@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] source-export-native-lease
Only trusted absolute argv accepted; a stable private lock is acquired before
starting the sender. FD 4 acknowledges only after sender registration; disk
bytes flow directly to inherited stdout, never into the control protocol. EOF,
malformed control, cancellation, excessive diagnostics or the monotonic lease
deadline kill and reap the sender before exit. Only valid L<millis> frames may
renew a lease, bounded to 300 seconds; X revokes it. No utility diagnostics
escape. Success requires a successful sender exit and confirmed reaping.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] source-export-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover duration/refusal bounds, control-frame renewal
semantics, reaping order and diagnostics bounds. Real transport behavior stays
with the disposable NixOS transfer fixtures that drive a sender process on a
real pool, and with differential wire sessions against the C helper.
